Mike, you can say anything you want, but Carol's getting me a bike.

252
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:14,140
Uh -huh. Boys bike or girls?

253
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:21,660
Done! Bye, Mom!

254
00:14:21,740 --> 00:14:23,300
Bye, Dad! Have fun time shopping!

255
00:14:23,460 --> 00:14:24,160
Take your time.

256
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:26,360
I'll keep my eye on Ben and what's -his -name.

257
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:36,660
Carol, come on!

258
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:37,720
I'm dribbling here!

259
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:39,060
So you eat your sleep.

260
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:44,000
Oh, you think you're real slick with this raffle thing, don't you?

261
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:46,720
But you can just kid yourself that you're doing all this for little Ben.

262
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:48,460
You know, you don't fool me, Carol.

263
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:52,560
I know you're just doing this because for once in your pathetic life, you see a

264
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:53,620
chance to top me.

265
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:54,800
Oh, sorry, Mike.

266
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:55,680
Were you speaking to me?

267
00:14:56,660 --> 00:14:58,880
You know, I think it's really cruel the way you're using Ben.

268
00:14:59,340 --> 00:15:03,180
Yeah, well, I guess I don't have as much experience in using people as you do.

269
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:05,880
That's right. I mean, no.

270
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:09,580
Face it, Ben, you blew it.

271
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:13,480
I told you we were gonna mess up, but did you listen?

272
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:16,540
What happened? Jody, what'd he do?

273
00:15:16,700 --> 00:15:18,780
He just ruined the whole raffle, that's all.

274
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:22,700
What? He sold the first two tickets to the Babots brothers.

275
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:27,400
So? So they put the word out, if anybody else buys a ticket, they'll pound them.

276
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:31,520
So you only sold two tickets?

277
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:32,940
No, I bought one too.

278
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,700
The Babotses don't scare me.

279
00:15:35,520 --> 00:15:38,400
So, you're selling your bike for three dollars?

280
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:40,400
Two fifty. I got a discount.

281
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:43,260
Carol, what do I do?

282
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:44,340
What do I do?

283
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:48,120
Yes, Carol. What's the next step in your can't lose raffle scheme?

284
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:50,980
This is impossible.

285
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:52,500
I mean, totally and completely.

286
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:54,520
I calculated all the probabilities.

287
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:58,680
Yeah, right. I'd be glad to help you, Ben.

288
00:15:59,420 --> 00:16:02,360
You will? Thank you, thank you, thank you!

289
00:16:03,780 --> 00:16:05,680
But first thing we gotta do is get rid of Carol.

290
00:16:06,260 --> 00:16:08,700
Carol who? Dad!

291
