308
00:16:57,800 --> 00:16:59,920
Ben, we expected you to earn that money.

309
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:01,480
Hey, we all did.

310
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:05,420
But I think that the little guy here knows that what he did was wrong, right, Ben?

311
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:08,820
Mike. This should certainly not go unpunished.

312
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:14,580
What? I think that a fitting punishment is for you two fine parents to just call

313
00:17:14,580 --> 00:17:15,600
this whole raffle thing off.

314
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:19,220
And you should tell any kid that comes up here that Ben is now raffling off his old

315
00:17:19,220 --> 00:17:21,500
bike, and, uh, you should give them their money back.

316
00:17:22,860 --> 00:17:24,040
Yes, I'm guilty.

317
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:24,800
I did it.

318
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:27,280
Punish me. Who want Mike or Ben?

319
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:30,720
I took Mike last time.

320
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:33,220
Mike, come with me.

321
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:36,400
Mom, I'm an innocent bystander here.

322
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:38,520
Sure. I am, Carol.

323
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:39,260
Would you say something?

324
00:17:39,940 --> 00:17:41,960
I have a lot of studying to do.

325
00:17:42,260 --> 00:17:44,080
Carol, I'm waiting.

326
00:17:45,820 --> 00:17:46,960
She's waiting, Mike.

327
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:51,160
Oh, fine. Why is it every time something goes wrong in this house, I'm always the

328
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:52,480
one who gets blamed for it?

329
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:54,880
How many kids do you have to pay back?

330
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:59,180
Three. You're gonna raffle your bike for three bucks?

331
00:18:00,060 --> 00:18:01,580
$2.50. I got a discount.

332
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:05,060
Mike, how many times do we have to cover this?

333
00:18:05,220 --> 00:18:06,200
You know Ben worships you.

334
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:09,840
You know he'll follow your lead no matter how stupid or scatterbrained your idea is.

335
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:12,320
Mom... Don't you take that tone with me, young man.

336
00:18:13,580 --> 00:18:14,200
Raffles are illegal.

337
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:16,480
You could have gotten our little Ben thrown in the slammer.

338
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:18,060
Mom, first of all, I agree.

339
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:20,140
It was an incredibly stupid idea.

340
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:22,640
Oh, progress. But the idea wasn't mine.

341
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:23,780
Oh, come on, Mike.

342
00:18:23,780 --> 00:18:26,100
Ben isn't sophisticated enough to come up with something like this.

343
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:28,320
I know. Then whose idea was it?

344
00:18:28,380 --> 00:18:30,040
Carol's. Ha! Carol Siever.

345
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:32,600
Yes. Mom, I'm going over to Debbie's.

346
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:34,020
I'll probably stay for dinner.

347
00:18:34,980 --> 00:18:37,540
In fact, there's a good chance I'll stay overnight.

348
00:18:38,220 --> 00:18:40,400
Bye, sweetheart. She's getting away!

349
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:43,680
Mike, you are only making things worse for yourself.

350
00:18:43,740 --> 00:18:46,640
Mom, I tried to talk Ben and Carol out of this all along.

351
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:52,320
So you expect me to believe that it was Carol's idea that Ben have an illegal raffle

352
00:18:52,320 --> 00:18:55,570
and the the whole time you were the voice of reason as you tried desperately to

353
00:18:55,570 --> 00:18:57,150
convince them that what they were doing was wrong?

354
00:18:59,670 --> 00:19:01,670
I believe I have the right to an attorney.

355
00:19:07,050 --> 00:19:09,530
Ben, that bike cost us 75 bucks.

356
00:19:10,690 --> 00:19:12,050
Okay, Steve -er -head.

357
00:19:14,730 --> 00:19:16,490
The Babots boys are here.

358
00:19:16,730 --> 00:19:20,850
Yeah. Gentlemen. Oh, hi, sir.

359
00:19:20,850 --> 00:19:22,250
You think you're conducting the raffle?

360
00:19:23,590 --> 00:19:25,910
The raffle's canceled, you dirtbags.

361
00:19:26,230 --> 00:19:28,230
What? Yeah. Hold it, Todd.

362
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:31,850
Wait, Vinnie. You know, I think a better punishment for you might be to just go

363
00:19:31,850 --> 00:19:34,310
ahead with this raffle, and you can just say goodbye to your bike.

364
00:19:34,770 --> 00:19:36,090
What? No, Dad.

365
00:19:36,330 --> 00:19:38,410
As a matter of fact, you can pick the winning ticket, all right?

366
00:19:39,090 --> 00:19:41,110
Come on, you'll make some kid very happy.

367
00:19:43,410 --> 00:19:44,850
And the winner is...

368
00:19:47,150 --> 00:19:48,870
number three. I won!

369
00:19:48,910 --> 00:19:50,470
I won! I won!

370
00:19:51,030 --> 00:19:52,730
You're gonna get it, Joey.

371
00:19:53,010 --> 00:19:54,470
Wait a minute now.

372
00:19:54,470 --> 00:19:56,510
We don't threaten young ladies here, Vinnie.

373
00:19:57,010 --> 00:19:57,850
Say hi, Vinnie.

374
00:19:58,190 --> 00:19:59,410
I'm Todd. I don't care.

375
00:19:59,450 --> 00:20:00,370
Get out of here.

376
00:20:03,770 --> 00:20:06,110
Jason, we've got someone to talk to.

377
00:20:06,350 --> 00:20:06,870
Oh, come on.

378
00:20:06,870 --> 00:20:08,570
You said you'd take Mike this time.

379
00:20:08,710 --> 00:20:09,710
It wasn't Mike.

380
00:20:10,310 --> 00:20:11,030
It was Carol.

381
00:20:11,630 --> 00:20:13,950
What? Yeah, we're all pretty stunned.

382
00:20:15,370 --> 00:20:17,650
Come on. Not our Carol.

383
00:20:17,750 --> 00:20:18,750
Carol Zeber? Yeah.

384
00:20:20,630 --> 00:20:23,230
Gee, Jody, I'm pretty glad you won the bike.

385
00:20:23,590 --> 00:20:26,170
Because since we're best friends and everything, I know you'll give it back.

386
00:20:26,370 --> 00:20:27,390
Yeah, Ben, right.

387
00:20:31,730 --> 00:20:33,430
Eh, I could have warned you about women.

388
00:20:34,270 --> 00:20:35,850
I should have never gone to Carol.

389
00:20:36,310 --> 00:20:37,210
Hey, you learning?

390
00:20:37,530 --> 00:20:39,810
I only did it because you were using me.

391
00:20:39,990 --> 00:20:45,010
How? Waxing your car, doing your chores, shining your shoes, ironing your...

392
00:20:45,010 --> 00:20:46,550
Okay, okay, okay.

393
00:20:46,570 --> 00:20:48,170
Maybe I have learned a lesson here too.

394
00:20:48,910 --> 00:20:51,930
What? Maybe the ironing was a little too much.

395
00:20:53,050 --> 00:20:54,530
I thought I liked the ironing.

396
00:20:55,630 --> 00:20:59,190
We'll talk. How am I supposed to get my bike back from Jodie?

397
00:20:59,770 --> 00:21:02,130
Well, I am fairly skilled at handling women.

398
00:21:02,690 --> 00:21:03,490
You'd help me?

399
00:21:04,250 --> 00:21:05,450
Of course, you're my brother.

400
00:21:05,830 --> 00:21:06,530
Yeah, you're right.

401
00:21:06,550 --> 00:21:07,510
Who needs Carol?

402
00:21:07,870 --> 00:21:11,510
Yeah, you know, I think she was onto something with this raffle thing though.

403
00:21:11,510 --> 00:21:13,210
She just didn't know how to make it work for her.

404
00:21:13,570 --> 00:21:14,890
I don't get it.

405
00:21:15,570 --> 00:21:16,730
Let me explain it to you, bro.

406
00:21:17,330 --> 00:21:22,370
See, although a good idea is important, what really counts is what you do with it.

407
00:21:22,690 --> 00:21:26,130
See, you gotta ask yourself, what is it that everyone really wants?

408
00:21:31,630 --> 00:21:35,470
Well, Carol, we just hope that doing kitchen duty for a month will teach you that

409
00:21:35,470 --> 00:21:36,590
it's wrong to run scams.

410
00:21:37,570 --> 00:21:41,990
Mom, for the first time in my life, I messed up, got in trouble, and I'm getting

411
00:21:41,990 --> 00:21:44,790
severely punished. Why do you sound so happy?

412
00:21:45,830 --> 00:21:51,950
Well, frankly, I found the whole thing, I don't know, interesting.

413
00:21:52,810 --> 00:21:57,110
Interesting? Yeah, kind of exciting.

414
00:21:58,010 --> 00:21:59,430
Are you saying?

415
00:21:59,570 --> 00:22:01,950
The planning, the danger, the execution.

416
00:22:02,910 --> 00:22:08,270
I guess I know now why Mike finds delinquent behavior so delicious.

417
00:22:08,270 --> 00:22:15,570
Yes. You know, Mike has a real capacity to just...

418
00:22:15,570 --> 00:22:17,510
I know. And Ben...

419
00:22:17,510 --> 00:22:18,430
Is on his way.

420
00:22:19,810 --> 00:22:21,710
So if we lose Carol, too...

421
00:22:21,710 --> 00:22:22,950
We're outnumbered.

422
00:22:25,550 --> 00:22:27,450
We better have another baby quick.

423
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:59,510
I'm gonna be a star I'm gonna be a star I'm gonna be a star I'm gonna be a star I'm

424
00:22:59,510 --> 00:23:08,050
gonna be a star I'm gonna be a star I'm gonna be a star I'm gonna be a star
